        {"kind": "h2", "text": "7.4 Constraints & Assumptions"},
        {"kind": "bullets", "items": [
            "Constraint: stdio transport only, so each server runs on the same machine as the MCP client.",
            "Constraint: one credential set per server process, at whatever privilege that credential holds. There is no per-tool authorization layer.",
            "Constraint: every server is bounded by upstream rate limits, quotas, and data-freshness lags that HaorGrix does not control.",
            "Assumption: the operator reviews consequential agent actions rather than running fully unattended, which is why guards are confirmations rather than policy engines.",
            "Assumption: the machine running these servers is trusted and its environment variables are not readable by third parties.",
            "Assumption: usage stays within the free or already-paid tiers of the upstream APIs, so no incremental API cost is expected.",
        ]},
