        {"kind": "h1", "text": "8. Design & UX"},
        {"kind": "para", "text": "These are headless servers. There is no GUI, no wireframe, and no design system. The design surface is the tool catalogue itself, because a tool name, its description, and its JSON schema are the entire affordance an agent has for deciding what to call."},
        {"kind": "bullets", "items": [
            "Naming: tools should be prefixed by server (brevo_, cp_, ga_, wp_) so names stay unique when several servers are mounted at once. Two servers do not yet follow this and are covered by FR-4.",
            "Descriptions: each description must state what the tool does, whether it mutates anything, and any precondition — for example that wp_get_post_meta requires the Agent Cache Control mu-plugin, or that submit_url_for_indexing requires Owner permission.",
            "Errors: failures should name the failing tool, the upstream status, and what the operator can do about it, with credentials redacted. An unadorned upstream JSON blob forces the agent to guess.",
            "Guard ergonomics: a confirmation gate should be a literal string the agent must repeat (as brevo_schedule_campaign requires confirm=\"SCHEDULE\"), so that satisfying it is a deliberate act rather than a default-filled boolean.",
            "Edge-case states: empty results, partial pagination, and truncated result sets must be reported explicitly. Silently returning a capped list reads to an agent as a complete one.",
        ]},

