        {"kind": "h2", "text": "9.2 Rollout Strategy"},
        {"kind": "bullets", "items": [
            "Phased rollout: there is no feature-flag infrastructure. A server is rolled out by updating the MCP client config to point at the new build; the previous build remains on disk.",
            "Migration: no data migration is involved, since the servers hold no state. Tool renames under FR-4 ship with the old name retained as a deprecated alias for one release so agent prompts and saved workflows do not break on upgrade.",
            "Rollback: revert the MCP client config to the prior entrypoint, or `git checkout` the previous commit and rebuild. Rollback does not undo upstream writes already performed — those must be reversed on the platform itself, which is precisely why the guards in FR-5 matter.",
            "Deprecated versions are moved to archive/ rather than deleted, as was done for Meta Ads v1.",
        ]},
