        {"kind": "h1", "text": "12. Legal, Privacy & Compliance"},
        {"kind": "table", "header": ["Area", "Consideration", "Owner / Status"], "rows": [
            ["Data privacy", "Personal data flows through Brevo contacts and email engagement, WooCommerce customers and orders, and GA4/GSC analytics. The servers add no storage of their own, but tool results enter an agent's context window and any transcript retained there.", "Musfiqur Tuhin — needs review"],
            ["Security review", "Completed 2026-07-22 for the committed-secret finding; history purged. A threat model covering the two escape-hatch tools and the absence of write guards has not been done.", "Musfiqur Tuhin — partially complete"],
            ["Regulatory / compliance", "GDPR and CCPA apply to client contact and customer data. No SOC 2 or HIPAA scope. PCI is not implicated: WooCommerce order tools read order metadata, not cardholder data, which the payment gateway holds.", "TBD — needs confirmation per client"],
            ["Legal / contractual", "Use of each platform is bound by its own API terms. Client authorisation to operate their property via automation should be explicit in the engagement terms.", "TBD — needs confirmation"],
            ["Data retention & deletion", "No server-side retention. The audit log is local and currently unbounded — a retention period should be set before it is extended to all six servers.", "Musfiqur Tuhin — open"],
        ]},

        {"kind": "break"},
        {"kind": "h1", "text": "13. Risks, Dependencies & Open Questions"},
        {"kind": "h2", "text": "13.1 Risks & Mitigations"},
        {"kind": "table", "header": ["Risk", "Likelihood", "Impact", "Mitigation"], "rows": [
            ["The two Google service-account keys committed to git history are used by an unauthorised party before rotation.", "L", "H", "History was purged and the repository is private and was never public. Rotate both keys by 2026-08-15 and review Google Cloud audit logs for unexpected access."],
            ["An agent invokes a destructive tool in cpanel-mcp or wordpress-mcp on a misread instruction — dropping a database, deleting a user, removing a DNS record.", "M", "H", "Implement FR-5 guard parity. Until then, keep those servers mounted only for supervised sessions."],
            ["An agent creates and activates Meta ad entities, incurring real spend.", "L", "H", "Writes already refuse unless META_ALLOW_WRITES is set. Keep it unset by default and enable only for a specific supervised task."],
            ["cp_uapi_call or wp_rest_request is used to reach an operation that has no typed guardrail at all.", "M", "H", "Treat both as break-glass. Restrict or remove them once the typed tool coverage is judged sufficient; log every invocation."],
            ["A change to one of five untested servers breaks it silently and the failure only surfaces mid-task on a client property.", "H", "M", "Implement the smoke tests in FR-9; run typecheck in CI on every push."],
            ["cp_delete_dns_record and cp_remove_cron key on brittle identifiers (line number, exact command string), so a concurrent edit causes the wrong record to be deleted.", "M", "M", "Re-read and verify the target immediately before deletion; prefer content-matched identification over positional."],
            ["Unprefixed tool names in two servers collide with another server's tools when mounted together, causing the wrong platform to be called.", "M", "M", "Implement FR-4 name normalisation with deprecated aliases."],
            ["An upstream API version deprecation breaks a server without warning.", "M", "M", "Pin versions where the platform allows it (META_API_VERSION), and subscribe to each vendor's deprecation notices."],
            ["A pagination cap silently truncates a result set and the agent reports a partial answer as complete.", "M", "M", "Return an explicit truncation flag whenever a cap is hit, and state it in the tool description."],
            ["Single-maintainer concentration: all six servers depend on one engineer.", "H", "M", "The PRD set itself is the mitigation. Add per-server READMEs and tests so a second engineer can pick one up."],
        ]},
        {"kind": "h2", "text": "13.2 Open Questions"},
        {"kind": "table", "header": ["Question", "Owner", "Status"], "rows": [
            ["When will the two compromised Google service-account keys be rotated, and has Cloud audit logging been reviewed for misuse in the interim?", "Musfiqur Tuhin", "Open"],
            ["Should cp_uapi_call and wp_rest_request be kept as break-glass tools, restricted to an allowlist, or removed entirely?", "Musfiqur Tuhin", "Open"],
            ["What is the standard guard convention — a per-tool confirmation string, a server-level write-enable flag, or both depending on severity?", "Musfiqur Tuhin", "Open"],
            ["Do the unprefixed tools in google-search-console-mcp and mcp-meta-ads get renamed, and what is the deprecation window for the aliases?", "TBD — unassigned", "Open"],
            ["Who owns QA for this portfolio, given no QA lead is currently assigned?", "HaorGrix", "Open"],
            ["What retention period applies to the audit log once it covers all six servers, given it may contain client personal data?", "Musfiqur Tuhin", "Open"],
            ["Is client authorisation for automated operation of their properties explicit in current engagement terms?", "TBD — unassigned", "Open"],
        ]},
        {"kind": "h2", "text": "13.3 Decision Log"},
        {"kind": "table", "header": ["Date", "Decision", "Rationale", "Decided By"], "rows": [
            ["2026-07-07", "Consolidate all MCP servers into one repository rather than one repository per server.", "Sets credential handling, gitignore discipline, and release process once. The servers share an audience and a maintainer, and per-repo overhead would exceed the isolation benefit.", "Musfiqur Tuhin"],
            ["2026-07-21", "Rewrite the Meta Ads server as v2 instead of patching v1.", "v1 lacked pagination and complete insights coverage, and had no write guard. The surface area of the fix approached a rewrite.", "Musfiqur Tuhin"],
            ["2026-07-22", "Rewrite git history to purge the two committed service-account keys, rather than pushing as-is and rotating.", "Removes the secret from every commit before it reaches a hosted remote. Backup taken first; the four-commit history was preserved.", "Musfiqur Tuhin"],
            ["2026-07-22", "Keep Meta Ads v1 in archive/ rather than deleting it.", "Preserves the reference implementation for comparison without implying it is maintained.", "Musfiqur Tuhin"],
            ["2026-07-22", "Publish the monorepo as private, not public.", "It targets HaorGrix-specific operational platforms and client properties; there is no case for public distribution.", "Musfiqur Tuhin"],
        ]},

        {"kind": "h1", "text": "14. Appendix & Glossary"},
        {"kind": "h2", "text": "14.1 Competitive / Market Analysis"},
        {"kind": "para", "text": "Public MCP servers exist for several of these platforms — WordPress, Google Analytics, and Google Search Console all have community implementations, and Meta publishes its own Graph API tooling. They were not adopted for three reasons. First, coverage: the public servers implement a generic subset, whereas the HaorGrix servers implement the specific operations this business actually performs, such as Elementor CSS regeneration, multi-layer cache purging, and CTR-rescue analysis. Second, trust: these tools hold production credentials for client properties, and a third-party dependency in that position is a supply-chain exposure. Third, composability: the cross-server integration between cpanel-mcp and wordpress-mcp via the Agent Cache Control mu-plugin only works because both sides are owned."},
        {"kind": "para", "text": "The trade-off accepted is maintenance burden. A community server has more contributors than one engineer, and the portfolio's largest risk (section 13.1) is exactly that concentration."},
        {"kind": "h2", "text": "14.2 Glossary"},
        {"kind": "table", "header": ["Term", "Definition"], "rows": [
            ["MCP", "Model Context Protocol — an open protocol through which AI applications discover and invoke external tools."],
            ["stdio transport", "MCP carried over a child process's standard input and output, as opposed to HTTP or SSE. Requires client and server on the same machine."],
            ["Tool", "A named, JSON-schema-typed operation a server exposes. The unit of capability an agent selects and calls."],
            ["Read / write classification", "Whether a tool only retrieves data or mutates state on the upstream platform. Write tools are the ones requiring guards."],
            ["Escape hatch", "A tool accepting an arbitrary upstream call — cp_uapi_call, wp_rest_request. Maximally flexible and entirely unguarded."],
            ["Guard / gate", "A precondition on a destructive tool: a literal confirmation string the caller must repeat, or a server-level flag such as META_ALLOW_WRITES."],
            ["Dry-run", "A mode in which a write tool validates and reports what it would do without issuing the mutating upstream call. Implemented in brevo-mcp."],
            ["UAPI", "cPanel's User API, the interface cpanel-mcp wraps."],
            ["Application Password", "A WordPress credential for REST authentication. Carries the full privileges of its user and cannot be scoped per capability."],
            ["mu-plugin", "A WordPress must-use plugin, loaded automatically and not deactivatable from the admin UI. The Agent Cache Control helper is installed this way."],
            ["Apple MPP", "Apple Mail Privacy Protection, which pre-fetches images and inflates reported email open rates. brevo_campaign_report corrects for it."],
            ["BUC throttling", "Business Use Case rate limiting on the Meta Graph API, applied per ad account rather than per application."],
        ]},
